hi:18.back_translation:
Write a function that parses an Indian Railways ticket booking status string. Ignore case and leading/trailing whitespace; parts may be separated by "/" or spaces (one or more). Supported formats:
- Confirmed: "CNF/B2/45" or "CNF/B2/45/LB" -> {"status": "CNF", "coach": "B2", "berth": 45, "berth_type": "LB"}
  (None if berth_type is not present; return coach and berth_type in uppercase; berth is an int).
- RAC: "RAC 12" or "RAC/12" -> {"status": "RAC", "number": 12}
- Waitlist: "WL 34", "GNWL 34", "RLWL/5", "PQWL 2", "TQWL 9" -> {"status": "WL", "list": "GNWL", "number": 34}
  where list is the exact waitlist code written, in uppercase ("WL", "GNWL", "RLWL", "PQWL", or "TQWL").
Return None for anything else (including non-numeric berth/number).

hi:32.back_translation:
Write a function that validates and parses an Indian Corporate Identification Number (CIN). First strip and uppercase it.
A CIN consists of 21 characters: 1 character "L" (listed) or "U" (unlisted); a 5-digit industry code; a 2-letter state code;
4 digits of the year of incorporation (must be between 1850-2100); 3 letters of the company type, which must be one of these:
PLC, PTC, GOI, SGC, FLC, GAP, NPL, ULL, ULT, OPC; a 6-digit registration number.
Return {"listed": bool, "industry": "72200", "state": "MH", "year": 2010, "type": "PTC", "reg_no": "123456"}
(year an int, the rest strings), or None if invalid.

